Attribution and third-party components
================================================================================

1. Fast Radon Transform -- ALGORITHM (public-domain mathematics)
   The recursive-doubling discrete Radon transform implemented in
   streakradon/frt.py is an INDEPENDENT, clean-room implementation written from
   the published algorithm:
     * Gotz, W. A. & Druckmuller, H. J. (1996), "A fast digital Radon
       transform", Pattern Recognition 29, 711.
     * Brady, M. L. (1998), "A fast discrete approximation algorithm for the
       Radon transform", SIAM J. Comput. 27, 107.
     * Nir, G., Ofek, E. O., Ben-Ami, S. & Zackay, B. (2018), "Optimal and
       efficient streak detection in astronomical images", AJ 156, 229.
   It was implemented from the mathematics/equations in these papers and is NOT
   derived from any existing source implementation. Algorithms are not
   copyrightable; this file is an original work (c) 2026 Ryder H. Strauss.
   Please cite Nir et al. (2018) in scientific use.

2. pyradon -- REMOVED
   Earlier revisions vendored a pinned copy of github.com/guynir42/pyradon
   (Copyright (C) 2018 Guy Nir, GPLv3) as the detection backend. It has been
   REMOVED: streakradon now detects with its own clean-room frt.py (item 1). No
   third-party GPL source remains in the distribution. The Nir et al. (2018)
   algorithm reference is retained above as a scientific citation. See
   LICENSING.md for the (git) history and the relicensing note.

3. Trailed-source forward fit
   streakradon/trail_fit.py implements the line-convolved-Gaussian trail model of
   Veres, P. et al. (2012), "Improved asteroid astrometry and photometry with
   trail fitting", PASP 124, 1197. Original implementation (c) 2026 R. H. Strauss.

The heliolinx pipeline this feeds is a separate work with its own license.
